.TH Command REALM
.SY "realm <NUMBER> <SECTS>"
The realm command allows you to manipulate the contents of the
"realm"s associated with your country
which provide a convenient way to save coordinates that are
frequently used, (see "info syntax" for use of realm arguments).
.s3
In the syntax of the realm command
<NUMBER> is the number of the realm to be set.
Note that the update command manipulates realm 0 (see "info update").
.s1
The "<SECTS>" argument is optional; if included the specified realm will be
set to "<SECTS>"; if omitted the coordinates of the specified realm will
be printed.  e.g.
.sp
.EX realm 1
.NF
Realm 1 is -3:3,3:3
.FI
.EX realm 1 -3:2,4
.EX realm 1
.NF
Realm 1 is now set to -3:2,4:4
.FI
.s3
If the <NUMBER> argument is omitted the coordinates of all realms will be
printed.
.s3
Also note that the <SECTS> argument may use the "#" form of realm
specification.
.EX realm 0 #1
Now realm 0 is set to -3:2,4:4.
.s3
The nation report includes the coordinates of all four realms.
.s3
See also : syntax, nation, update
